I've written a patch that makes the following enhancements to
NetHack's mail-checking feature:

* You can check maildir-style mailboxes.
* You can check multiple mailboxes by specifying the MAILPATH
  environment variable.
* Tilde expansion works in the file names specified in the MAIL and
  MAILPATH environment variables.

My motivation, naturally, was to make enough improvements here to
allow NetHack to check my e-mail for me; I have multiple maildir-style
mailboxes, and my MAILPATH has tildes in it.

The patch doesn't affect save and bones compatibility and should apply
cleanly alongside other patches -- after all, src/mail.c is the only
file touched by it (besides a paragraph in the Guidebook).

You can download the maildirpath patch from:

http://web.ics.purdue.edu/~kuliniew/nethack/maildirpath.html

Since this is the first patch I've written for NetHack, I'd appreciate
any comments on it, even nitpicky style issues and the like.

Once any remaining bugs are found and fixed, I plan on submitting this
to the DevTeam.

Enjoy!

